{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan authored and reviewed to PASS (0 blocking, 1 minor P6 advisory), 1 round, signed at HEAD 1052bc856f.\n\nEvery reported claim CONFIRMED against the tree:\n- _referencing_commit_exists (transition_close.py:149) runs git log with NO ref\n  (:159-163), scans HEADs whole reachable history, and accepts a rebar-ticket: trailer or\n  leading <id>: subject resolving to the ticket or any transitive descendant (:170-176,\n  accepted_ids built at :277-286). Merge status never consulted.\n- The precheck is gated on recorded file_impact at transition_close.py:283-284.\n- transition --ref documented at src/rebar/_cli/help/transition.txt:7 and\n  docs/plan-review-gate.md:899-916; AGENTS.md mentions it zero times (grep -c -- \"--ref\" is 0).\n- The real ordering rule is the adjacent policy line at AGENTS.md:233-234 (Verified +1).\n- The stale passage is AGENTS.md:235-242; the NEVER-touch-the-shared-checkout warning at\n  :239-242 is preserved verbatim in the plan.\n\nThree additions the original analysis did not have, all folded into the plan:\n- The population is TWO files, not one. CONTRIBUTING.md:219-230 (2f) repeats the identical\n  misstatement, and AGENTS.md:203 points readers there for \"the full recipe\". Fixing only\n  AGENTS.md would leave the long-form authoritative copy wrong. Both are now in scope/file_impact.\n- The precheck has further exits the doc should not imply away: _completion_precheck (:195)\n  returns early when require_completion_verification_for_close is off (:228-236), on\n  --force-close (:237), and on a live duplicate/supersedes replacement link (:256).\n- --ref does NOT narrow the referencing-commit scan. It retargets the completion verification\n  and signature to that refs tree; _referencing_commit_exists still runs git log with no ref.\n  Conflating the two would substitute one wrong mechanism for another, so the plan states the\n  distinction explicitly.\n\nChecked and clear: no test pins the replaced wording (test_codex_agent_guidance.py:11-13 slices a\nregion ending before line 235; the Serena tests read only the navigation table), and\ntemplates/AGENTS.md is unaffected because test_client_template_sync.py guards only the\nrebar-usage marker region, which forbids Gerrit content.\n\nSeparate defect observed while running this review, NOT ticketed: the review emitted\n\"plan-review Pass-2 verification contract violation ... {\\\"unexpected\\\": [0, 1, 2, 3]}\" from\nrebar.llm.plan_review.workflow_ops — every Pass-2 verification index was rejected as unexpected,\ndegrading all four findings to INDETERMINATE (verdict unchanged). Reproduced on the 0c49 review\nrun at HEAD 1052bc856f. Worth its own ticket."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785688477371586001,"uuid":"788bb77a-85c6-4738-9dc2-a1c6bba1ac16"}